From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-eliza: keep the UFS PHY GDSC on across system suspend

On the Retroid Pocket Duo (Eliza) the first system suspend powers
gcc_ufs_phy_gdsc off in genpd_suspend_noirq; on resume genpd_resume_noirq
cannot power it back on ("gcc_ufs_phy_gdsc status stuck at 'off'"), the
UFS clocks and the PHY ref_aux clock then refuse to enable (-EBUSY),
ufshcd_reset_and_restore() fails and leaves the host in
UFSHCD_STATE_ERROR. From then on __ufshcd_wl_suspend() returns -EBUSY
(link off, error handler refuses to run in ERROR state), so every later
suspend aborts on ufs_device_wlun.

Keep the GDSC in PWRSTS_RET_ON so software never collapses it; the
hardware moves it to retention when CX drops in system sleep.


---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-eliza.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-eliza.c
@@ -2781,7 +2781,14 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "gcc_ufs_phy_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	/*
+	 * Never collapse from software: after a system sleep the GDSC does not
+	 * power back up in resume_noirq ("status stuck at 'off'"), the UFS host
+	 * fails to resume and is left in UFSHCD_STATE_ERROR, which aborts every
+	 * later suspend with -EBUSY. The hardware still drops it to retention
+	 * when CX goes down, as for the USB GDSCs on Milos.
+	 */
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 };
 
